  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TELLING\n\nA robot trained to train a\nrobot to TELL ITS THING.\n\nThe pedestal beside the desk\nis the perch. On a thing\u2019s\npanel it holds a bird to\nthat thing; out here it\nholds a bird of your own,\nto the nest \u201cwhat it told\u201d.\n\nA letter put on the perch\ngoes to whichever bird\nstands there."
   },
   "x": -1.15,
   "z": 2.25
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TO RUN IT\n\nGive the four-hole box to\nthe teacher and press Start.\n\nWatch the pupil take a desk,\ncopy the [set | value | _]\nletter, put the reading in\nit and give it to the bird\non the perch: it lands on\n\u201cwhat it told\u201d as\n[set | value | 5]."
   },
   "x": -0.45,
   "z": 2.25
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "THEN, ON A PANEL\n\nTake a number from the\nstack. Open its panel with\nthe gear, and drop on the\npanel a copy of the box and\nthe trained pupil.\n\nPress SPACE on the number:\nthe pupil runs on the\nnumber\u2019s own panel, and the\nbird on the perch there is\na bird to the number. It\nreads 5 now."
   },
   "x": 0.25,
   "z": 2.25
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "WHY THE PERCH\n\nThe pupil never learned\nwhat it tells. It learned\n\u201cgive the letter to the bird\non the perch\u201d, and the perch\nmeans the thing whose panel\nit is on.\n\nThat is what makes a\nbehaviour: the same robot,\nthe same box, on any thing."
   },
   "x": 0.95,
   "z": 2.25
  }
